post_install() {
  cat <<'NOTE'

  jarvis is installed, but it is only the program. The voices, the wake models and
  the python venv are large and fetched, so they are NOT in the package:

    jarvis setup          # Piper voices, wake models, the venv

  The Control Center / Touch Bar plugin is a template — pacman may not write into
  your $HOME:

    cp -r /usr/share/jarvis/plugin ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/macarchy.jarvis

  Then:
    systemctl --user enable --now jarvis-tick.timer jarvis-inbox.path

  If the mascot never appears on the Touch Bar, the module failed to load:
    journalctl --user -u macarchy-touchbar -b | grep 'failed to load'

NOTE
}

post_upgrade() {
  # A rename in macarchy-touchbar breaks the INSTALLED copy of the touchbar
  # module, and the daemon says so exactly once and then runs without it.
  macarchy-touchbar reload >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
}

pre_remove() {
  systemctl --user disable --now jarvis-tick.timer jarvis-inbox.path 2>/dev/null || true
}
